            <ArticleTitle>Temporal arteritis: don't let this disease fool you.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Temporal arteritis is a disease of older individuals that manifests with variable signs, symptoms, and pain in the head and jaw. This disease should be considered in the differential diagnosis if the dentist encounters a patient with puzzling complaints that are not explained by oral and physical findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
